# What `gcloud builds submit .` must NOT upload. Without this file gcloud falls back to
# .gitignore, which happens to exclude the release payloads too - but by accident, and a future
# .gitignore edit would silently start shipping 1.9 GB of them to Cloud Build. The image needs
# api/, data/verify_release.py and RELEASES.md and nothing else (api/Dockerfile); the release
# reaches the service from GCS at start (api/start.sh), never through the build.
.git/
.gitignore
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
data/releases/
data/receipts.json
assistant/
eval/
api/tests/
web/
tiles/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
api/.env
